+# Fresh independent GENERAL review, HG-044
+
+Reviewed implementation/result revision: `19dc5a4f8edc8869873a76a4fe27b0280761d7c9`.
+Protected base: `fa729ca4bcca0f2c2e7a2aa0601890d1356b8842`.
+Selected tested revision: `0af358014182c957eec07763aaaf9181d3e2d0c1`.
+
+The complete protected-base diff adds prospective mechanical M3 closure support only.
+The governance record supplies the task contract rather than a feature task packet.
+The indexed closure contract and delimited plan addendum preserve exactly 16 M3
+integration identities, separate M1 KL-074 support and recursively validated M2/M1.
+The validator traverses every declared prerequisite and requires the prerequisite
+merge before both consumer base and tested revisions. Integration, result, review,
+raw log and regression evidence resolve as hashed regular Git blobs at exact reachable
+revisions; a closure instance itself must be an unchanged regular HEAD blob. The
+reader parses the checked Git blob after validation rather than re-reading ambient
+bytes. Duplicate JSON keys fail closed.
+
+Every exit witness binds one exact unique named check, pinned whole check contract,
+command, PASS, result tested SHA, canonical oracle hash, result and raw evidence.
+The fresh regression requires the exact ordered commands at one fully integrated
+tested revision, successful integer-zero executions, hashed logs/collection/JUnit,
+nonempty successful case counts and equality between collected and executed cases.
+The repaired per-selector loop additionally requires a case for every declared
+selector. Thus unrelated successful cases cannot hide an omitted multi-suite
+selector. Both run and collection exits require `type(exit_code) is int`, rejecting
+JSON false and floating-point zero.
+
+The 31-row boundary ledger is projected exactly from canonical KL-028 authority,
+with only 19 planned executable rows becoming PASS and all 12 deferred layers
+retained NOT_RUN. B04 full TEST reauthorization remains deferred despite mandatory
+guard support; eight actual API/workflow/DB/rendering E2E layers, B11/B12 pure state
+evaluators and B14 worker/fault evidence remain deferred. The interleaving ledger
+has exactly nine DC PASS rows plus I04@WF NOT_RUN. PU equality stays PU, original
+reach labels remain intact, and shadow usability/R04 E2E remain NOT_RUN. Schema
+constants prevent production activation, executable shadow, product requirement
+PASS or reproduced historical model claims.
+
+The implementation leaves frozen Protocol/DB semantics, production source,
+migrations, DB lifecycle, CI, task definitions, existing M1/M2/HG043 validators and
+existing M1/M2 schema branches unchanged. All prior existing validator function
+source is identical except the intentionally scoped governance allowlist and main
+validation orchestration. The complete plan prefix before the new addendum is
+identical to protected base. Historical failed reviews and interrupted r2 raw
+material remain retained and unselected; the selected evidence round is fresh at
+the refreshed protected base.
+
+The previously recorded GENERAL selector-coverage blocker and integer-exit
+hardening finding are resolved by the reviewed implementation. Review-created raw
+files are only independent review bookkeeping and supply no task test authority.
+Applicable final hosted isolated PostgreSQL CI and all required specialist reviews
+remain separate gates; this review neither records MERGED nor creates M3 closure.
+No local database or foreign fixture lifecycle was run.
+
+This fresh round is **CHANGES_REQUIRED** for a newly reproduced regression-oracle
+blocker. Current actual harness/unit collection contains 25 parameter IDs where
+`::` occurs inside the parameter suffix. Pytest's installed `mangle_test_address`
+partitions at `[` before splitting the address and then restores the entire
+parameter suffix. HG044 splits the full node ID, producing different expected
+JUnit classname/name pairs. A complete synthetic integrated Git chain has an empty
+error list with valid baseline evidence; replacing only its harness case with one
+actual current parameter ID and correct pytest JUnit addressing produces exactly
+`milestone-m3-regression:incomplete-executed-collection`. All command-set, integer
+exit, hash, freshness, selector and successful-case-count checks still pass.
+
+The collection disposition regex also scans node records. Current actual collected
+parameter text contains `1 error`/`1 skipped` strings, and a successful parameter
+case named `[1 skipped]` is rejected as `collection-oracle`. Parameter content is
+not an execution or collection disposition. Both behaviors prevent valid required
+fresh regression evidence from satisfying the prospective contract. Normalize
+addresses using pytest's parameter-aware convention and inspect collection
+summary/error records separately from node text. Preserve the strict complete
+selector and failed/skip/error oracles, and add actual pytest-generated collection
+and JUnit coverage with both `::` and summary-looking parameter IDs. A repair needs
+new selected implementation evidence and a fresh exact-SHA review.
