+review={'task_identity':'harness-governance-v0.1/HG-044','reviewed_head_sha':HEAD,'review_type':'GENERAL','status':'CHANGES_REQUIRED','review_contract_version':'v0.2','protected_base_sha':BASE,'summary':'Fresh independent GENERAL review found a new blocker: the fresh-regression oracle rejects valid current pytest parameterized collection/JUnit evidence. Prior selector-coverage and integer-exit findings are resolved; scope, exact evidence bindings, legacy semantics and deferred layer dispositions remain preserved.','findings':[{'finding_id':'HG044-GENERAL-R3-001','classification':'BLOCKER','severity':'BLOCKER','priority':1,'title':'Accept valid parameter IDs when correlating collection with JUnit','file':'tools/harness/validate_harness.py','start':2643,'end':2655,'body':'The required fresh full-harness regression cannot validate existing successful pytest cases. Current real harness/unit collection has 25 parameter IDs containing :: inside brackets; line 2650 splits those parameter suffixes, whereas pytest partitions at [ before splitting and restores the complete suffix. On an otherwise valid full-command integrated Git fixture, replacing only the harness case with one actual current node ID and correct pytest JUnit addressing yields exactly milestone-m3-regression:incomplete-executed-collection. Lines 2645-2646 also scan node text for error/skip disposition words; current collected parameter text includes 1 error/1 skipped, and successful [1 skipped] parameter evidence yields exactly collection-oracle. Baseline validation returns no errors, and all hash/freshness, integer-zero, selector and successful-count guards pass in both reproductions. These false rejections block the mandatory integrated regression without changing frozen semantics.','required_change':'Normalize node addresses according to pytest parameter-aware JUnit addressing: split only the nonparameter address and preserve the entire bracket suffix. Check collection disposition/summary records separate